\image(figures/one_r_titanic.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Training-only selected Titanic rule, identical-split ZeroR evaluation and raw held-out OneR confusion counts.)
\alttext(The fitting pass uses624 training labels;267 separate test labels contribute only to evaluation. The chart reports counts rather than concealing class imbalance in one overall accuracy.)

> Unseen categories and complete input contracts

The following model is trained on feature0→class0 and feature1→class1. Its tied
global training majority chooses0. Evaluating on a cohort containing mostly true
class1 does not change that fallback. An unseen feature2 therefore still
predicts0, even when the evaluation majority differs. The empty evaluation
convention returns zero rows/counts without defining an empirical accuracy.

Complete matching feature/label counts and rectangular shape are checked before
training/evaluation. Nonempty fitting requires at least one column. Empty
fitting returns a normalized empty model(total0/errors0/training accuracy0), and
attempting to predict from it throws. A prediction row must contain the selected
index; a malformed or inconsistent model is rejected. The DataFrame adapter
requires distinct nonresponse predictor names and finite integral int-range
cells; it performs no dropping or rounding.

For D attributes and N rows, nested ordered maps cost O(DN log N) work and O(N)
candidate state plus the selected rule. The optional history owns original
entriesND+N, candidate records, bucket class-count pairs and the selected map.
Its logical quota counts ND+N+2R plus each candidate1 and each bucket1+2K;
default1000000 and zero disables it. Admission precedes retained copies and
appends, with no partial trace on failure. This policy is not bytes, node
allocation cost or peak RAM. Prediction costs O(log V) for V selected feature
values; no training data or caller references remain in the model.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/one_r_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/one_r.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto model = dm::algorithms::one_r_train({{0}, {1}}, {0, 1});
    std::vector<dm::algorithms::OneREvaluation> evaluations{
        dm::algorithms::one_r_evaluate(model, {{0}, {1}}, {0, 1}),
        dm::algorithms::one_r_evaluate(model, {{2}, {2}, {1}}, {1, 1, 1}),
        dm::algorithms::one_r_evaluate(model, {}, {})
    };
    std::vector<std::string> labels{"seen values", "unseen and shifted",
                                    "empty evaluation"};
    std::vector<double> fallbacks;
    std::print("Frozen training fallback remains {}.\n\n", model.default_class);
    std::print("| evaluation control | actual evaluated rows | actual correct rows | actual fallback rows " "|\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < evaluations.size(); ++i) {
        auto &e = evaluations[i];
        fallbacks.push_back(e.fallbacks);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", labels[i], e.rows, e.correct,
                   e.fallbacks);
    }
    auto p =
        dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(fallbacks, labels, "actual unseen fallback");
    p.title("OneR fixed-model controls: unseen values never refit").x_label(
        "explicit evaluation cohort").y_label("actual frozen-fallback predictions").save_svg("build/one_r_controls.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Frozen training fallback remains 0.

| evaluation control | actual evaluated rows | actual correct rows | actual fallback rows |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| seen values | 2 | 2 | 0 |
| unseen and shifted | 3 | 1 | 2 |
| empty evaluation | 0 | 0 | 0 |
\image(figures/one_r_controls.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual frozen-model predictions under seen values, unseen categories, a changed class mix and empty evaluation.)
\alttext(Evaluation labels never refit the global fallback; unseen feature values keep the training-majority decision.)

> Verification

This ten-report batch passes 50 CTest cases, 25 directly instrumented ASan/UBSan
cases, 174 compiled and executed public examples, 707/707 scoped documentation
